MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Muddy Wolf at Red Rocks feels like a natural next choice because its blues focus connects with my recent interest in Memphis, Old Sock, and People, Hell & Angels.",
    "Led Zeppelin II and Hypnotic Eye also make sense: blues-driven guitar work appeals to me, and Tom Petty connects with my recent interest in Benmont Tench."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Blackstar's experimental direction does not fit my current desire for straightforward blues and roots rock, even though other rock albums appeal to me.",
    "Very Best Of, 25, and Live At Radio City Music Hall give me too little information about the music or performer to establish a connection with what I want today."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in guitar-centered rock seems to have been treated as a broader interest in rock releases, although the blues feel matters more to me right now.",
    "A collection or live recording is not appealing to me just because of its format; I need a reason to expect music that fits my interests."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The shared blues thread across Memphis, Old Sock, and People, Hell & Angels matters especially strongly to my choice today.",
    "An album can fit my interests without prompting me to choose it now. I rarely select much in one visit, and my curiosity about this live blues recording outweighs the other appealing options."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my interest in blues and roots-oriented rock, but some stretched that interest beyond the musical feel and clear connections that motivate me to choose an album today."
}
